        <body>
            <div xml:id="d717">

                <pb facs="1148" n="1052" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg1052"/>

                <head>No. 715.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Admiral Polo de
                            Bernabe to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Spain</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-01-03"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 3,
                        1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The undersigned, envoy extraordinary and minister plenipotentiary of Spain, while
                    having the honor to acknowledge the receipt of the note of the honorable
                    Secretary of State of the United States, of the 22d of December last, in which
                    it is declared that the Virginius at the time of her capture had no right to
                    carry the American flag, and did carry it wrongfully and improperly, must
                    express to the Secretary of State the satisfaction with which the government of
                    the Spanish Republic has been informed of this declaration, and that this
                    result, which was confidently expected, practically demonstrates that there was
                    no offense to the American flag, and that no intention to insult it ever could
                    or ever did exist.</p>
                <p>The undersigned avails himself of this opportunity to reiterate to the Hon.
                    Hamilton Fish the assurance of his highest consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>JOSÉ POLO DE BERNABÉ.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
